        "regime_read": "NQ leading / pulling away from ES \u2014 narrow, tech/AI-driven, FRAGILE. Trust directional moves less; watch for reversal when AI names cool.",
        "narrative": "Macro backdrop \u2014\n[2026-09-28] US economic state (FRED):\n  Growth: real GDP 1.5% (q/q ann)\n  Inflation: CPI 3.05% YoY | core CPI 2.22% | core PCE 2.92% (Fed target 2%)\n  Labor: unemployment 4.1%\n  Rates: fed funds 3.63% | 10Y 5.18% | 10Y-2Y 0.36% (NORMAL)\n  Consumer: UMich sentiment 51.7 | VIX 14.21\n\n---\nRecent market action has seen both ES and NQ futures pull back from their recent highs. The ES index is trading below its prior day's high, while the NQ index has pulled away from ES, indicating a narrow, tech/AI-driven concentration in the market. This suggests that any directional moves should be treated with caution due to the fragile nature of the current regime. Volume profiles for both indices show accumulation zones around their respective price-of-control (POC) levels: 7770.27 for ES and 30764.1 for NQ, indicating areas where significant buying interest is likely to be found or defended. The lead-lag analysis shows that the NQ index is leading, which implies a narrow market focus on tech/AI stocks. Given the current concentration regime, we should expect any moves in ES and NQ to be short-lived and potentially corrective. The upcoming FOMC event on September 30th will provide key data points for inflation, which could influence market sentiment. We are sizing into this with a long-the-dip bias, as the market is currently trading below its POC levels. However, if either index breaks below their respective POCs (7765 or 30750), we would need to reassess our position and potentially exit the trade.",
